{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>Blessed be Abram of El Most High</b> Seven verses in the Torah in which a blessing is written to the Holy One, blessed be He: וברוך ה' אלהי שם. וברוך אל עליון. ויאמר ברוך ה' אלהי אדני אברהם. ואקוד ואשתחוה לה' ואברך. ויאמר יתרו ברוך ה'. ואכלת ושבעת וברכת את ה'. ולגד אמר ברוך. And in them are 100 words, corresponding to the 100 blessings recited each day, and 7 verses corresponding to the 7 blessings of Shabbat and Yom Tov. And in five of them, the Name is adjacent to 'ברוך,' corresponding to the five books of the Torah, over which one must bless first. And if you add וברוך אל עליון with them, there are six, corresponding to the six sedarim."], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {0 "The phrase 'שבעה סדרים' likely refers to the six orders of the Mishnah; the text reads 'ששה סדרים' (six sedarim), translated as written."}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:16:09.694227682Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}